1- Prepare the Windows 10 Machine

Ensure the Windows VM is running.

Make sure it can reach the Wazuh Manager IP over the network.

Temporarily disable firewall if needed for testing.

2- Access Wazuh GUI

Open your browser and go to the Wazuh Manager GUI:

https://:(PortNumber)

Log in with your admin credentials.

3- Add a New Agent

In the Wazuh GUI, navigate to:

Management → Agents → Add agent

Fill in the agent details:

Agent name: Windows10-01 (or any descriptive name)

IP address:

Group: Optional (default is fine)

Manual registration key: Will be generated by the GUI

Click Add agent.

The GUI will display a registration command to run on the Windows agent.

4- Install the Agent on Windows

Copy the registration command from the Wazuh GUI.

Open PowerShell as Administrator on the Windows machine.

Paste and run the command. This installs and registers the agent with Wazuh Manager automatically.

5- Verify Connection

Back on the Wazuh GUI:

Go to Management → Agents

You should see the new agent listed as Active.

The agent is now ready to forward logs and receive detection rules.

